---
import { PLANS, formatKalVoiceAllowance } from "@kalcode/protocol/plans";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import XLink from "../components/XLink.astro";
import { getPage } from "../lib/site";

const page = getPage("/changelog");
const allowances = PLANS.map((plan) => `${plan.name} ${formatKalVoiceAllowance(plan.limits)}`).join(", ");
---
<Base title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <PageHead
    title="Changelog"
    lead="Development milestones and announcements for KalCode. Entries marked as development builds or in development have not been publicly released."
  />
  <section class="section" aria-label="Releases">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="release" aria-labelledby="release-website-2026-09-24">
        <div class="release__meta">
          <h2 class="release__version" id="release-website-2026-09-24">A new kalcoded.com and official X accounts</h2>
          <p><time datetime="2026-09-24">September 24, 2026</time></p>
          <p class="chip chip--built">Website · live</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            The website now shows KalCode instead of describing it. Every preview is labelled as a
            product preview with sample data, and anything not built yet says so.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Home.</strong> The animated KalCode symbol, the providers you already use with their honest adapter status, and the workspace in product previews: terminals, permissions, KalVoice and the Dashboard.</li>
            <li><strong>KalVoice page.</strong> One push-to-talk key (hold F8, speak, release), what happens to your words, KalVoice Requests per plan, and how audio stays on your device.</li>
            <li><strong>Pricing.</strong> One comparison table, with what every plan includes stated once.</li>
            <li><strong>Download.</strong> Build status for Windows, macOS and Linux, read from the release manifest. There is no public build yet, and the page says so.</li>
            <li><strong>Product.</strong> Each part of the workspace, with a table of what is built today and what is planned.</li>
            <li><strong>Official X accounts.</strong> Follow <XLink account="official" withHandle /> for KalCode news and <XLink account="founder" withHandle /> for the founder.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="release" aria-labelledby="release-kalvoice">
        <div class="release__meta">
          <h2 class="release__version" id="release-kalvoice">KalVoice and your own providers</h2>
          <p><time datetime="2026-09-24">September 24, 2026</time></p>
          <p class="chip chip--dev">Announcement · in development</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            KalVoice is the coding assistant and voice layer built into KalCode: speak your prompts,
            control your workspace, and coordinate your coding agents. It is in development and not
            part of any build yet.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Dictation.</strong> Hold the push-to-talk key (F8 by default), speak, and the text is typed into the focused input: a Claude Code, Codex or Gemini CLI thread, a terminal, or a search box. Speech recognition runs on your device; audio is not stored or uploaded. Unlimited on every plan.</li>
            <li><strong>Commands.</strong> With the same key, say a request such as “Open four Codex threads”. KalVoice decides from context whether you are dictating or giving a command. Structured commands run without any model; reasoning uses the provider you connected.</li>
            <li><strong>Bring your own provider.</strong> Claude Code, Codex and Gemini CLI run on your own accounts. KalCode does not charge for, resell or meter provider usage, and there is no KalCode-paid fallback.</li>
            <li><strong>Plan allowances.</strong> Plans now include KalVoice Requests each month ({allowances}). Every plan includes all provider connections, all permission modes and unlimited local dictation.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Read more in the <a href="/docs/kalvoice">KalVoice docs</a> and on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="release" aria-labelledby="release-0-1-0">
        <div class="release__meta">
          <h2 class="release__version" id="release-0-1-0">0.1.0 — Foundation</h2>
          <p><time datetime="2026-09-24">September 24, 2026</time></p>
          <p class="chip">Development build · not publicly released</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            The foundation every later part of KalCode builds on. There is nothing to download from
            this release; it exists so the next ones can be built on tested ground.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Desktop shell.</strong> The KalCode desktop app with its navigation shell, Dashboard and Settings.</li>
            <li><strong>Local SQLite persistence.</strong> One local database with versioned, checksummed migrations and a backup before each upgrade.</li>
            <li><strong>Typed event protocol.</strong> Every state change is a structured event, shared as generated types between the native runtime and the interface.</li>
            <li><strong>Structured logging.</strong> Local JSON logs with rotation and a redaction pass for credentials.</li>
            <li><strong>OS keychain secret storage.</strong> Credentials stored in the operating system's credential store, never in the database or logs.</li>
            <li><strong>Design system.</strong> Shared colours, typography and brand assets for the app and this website, in light and dark themes.</li>
            <li><strong>This website.</strong> kalcoded.com, with early-access registration.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
